1,"role":null}],"tags":["ios exploitation","coruna","optimizely","supply chain attack","caishen","darksword","mch control platform","card skimmer","caishen toolkit","third-party script compromise","cryptocurrency clipper"],"targeted_countries":[],"malware_families":["Caishen","Coruna","Darksword"],"attack_ids":["T1056.001","T1059.007","T1539","T1566.002","T1005","T1140","T1190","T1185","T1056.003","T1102","T1041","T1078","T1027","T1573","T1195.002","T1567.002","T1189","T1071.001","T1105","T1204.001"],"references":["https:\/\/censys.com\/blog\/mch-and-caishen-supply-chain-poisoning-pushes-ios-exploits"],"industries":["Media","Technology","Government","Finance","Retail","Hospitality"],"extract_source":[],"more_indicators":false},{"id":"6afcabb1c963ba9d1ae92e1a","name":"URGENT: iOS Exploits Are Being Actively Deployed via Poisoned JavaScript on BBC, Zoom, CNN and Other Major Websites","description":"Research reveals that threat actors have compromised third-party JavaScript providers including Optimizely, Kissmetrics, StorifyMe, and Minute-ly to deliver iOS exploits through at least 21 major websites. The attack routes Mobile Safari users to Coruna and DarkSword exploit-kit infrastructure without any user interaction. Affected sites span multiple sectors including BBC, CNN, Fox News, Zoom, GitLab, and Salesforce. Instead of targeting website backends directly, attackers poisoned widely-used analytics and content provider scripts, which then loaded malicious payloads that executed zero-click exploit chains. The compromised scripts operated via hidden iframes, leaving no visible indicators while exploiting vulnerabilities in Mobile Safari. This supply-chain attack bypasses traditional security measures as the malicious code originates from legitimate, trusted infrastructure that enterprise filters cannot block without disrupting business operations.","author_name":"AlienVault","modified":"2026-11-18T09:37:16.419000","created":"2026-11-17T19:32:01.613000","revision":2,"tlp":"white","public":1,"adversary":"","indicators":[{"id":4142369936,"indicator":"CVE-2022-48503","type":"CVE","created":"2026-11-17T19:32:02","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4587727825,"indicator":"http:\/\/webshell.lol\/get.js","type":"URL","created":"2026-11-17T19:32:02","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null}],"tags":["supply-chain","zero-click","exploit-kit","mobile safari","darksword","ios","coruna","third-party javascript"],"targeted_countries":[],"malware_families":["Coruna","DarkSword"],"attack_ids":["T1059.007","T1497.001","T1082","T1005","T1140","T1190","T1036","T1055","T1112","T1083","T1497","T1041","T1027","T1573","T1195.002","T1203","T1564.003","T1070.004","T1189","T1071.001"],"references":["https:\/\/zimperium.com\/blog\/urgent-ios-exploits-are-being-actively-deployed-via-poisoned-javascript-on-bbc-zoom-cnn-and-other-major-websites?hs_amp=true"],"industries":["Media","Technology","Finance","Telecommunications","Retail","Education"],"extract_source":[],"more_indicators":false},{"id":"6afd5c42c6e50b8c437fe592","name":"US Logistics Cyber Threats: 3 Campaigns & Defense","description":"Three distinct campaigns are actively targeting the US trucking and logistics sector through fraudulent business portals and malicious documents. HelloFriends uses fake FMCSA carrier verification portals to harvest credentials, SSNs, EINs, and fuel card information through phishing emails. NodeRemote distributes backdoors disguised as broker onboarding documents, establishing persistent access through scheduled tasks and rotating C2 infrastructure. Fake Freight Portals impersonate TIMOCOM and DAT platforms, delivering MeshCentral and CastleRAT through malicious WebDAV shortcuts while attempting to extract BitLocker recovery keys. These attacks exploit routine logistics workflows including carrier verification, broker onboarding, and freight booking. The campaigns demonstrate sophisticated social engineering, infrastructure rotation, and multi-stage infection chains that combine credential theft with persistent remote access capabilities.","author_name":"AlienVault","modified":"2026-11-18T09:35:24.992000","created":"2026-11-18T08:05:22.151000","revision":2,"tlp":"white","public":1,"adversary":"","indicators":[{"id":4510423918,"indicator":"87.120.104.213","type":"IPv4","created":"2026-11-18T08:05:22","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":"2026-12-18T08:00:00","is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4557241616,"indicator":"925a9d35a32e1a6a1ce1ae4b9ff09e289184d4d925d700752c99f15ab04296dd","type":"FileHash-SHA256","created":"2026-11-18T08:05:22","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4559141796,"indicator":"f74a0fbddac01f282b070fc6b57811a6","type":"FileHash-MD5","created":"2026-11-18T08:05:22","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4559141797,"indicator":"6a60d7fb542c4a603f982e8a6f0d6269188b2899","type":"FileHash-SHA1","created":"2026-11-18T08:05:22","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4587864425,"indicator":"dot.fmcsa.saferprofilereview.info","type":"hostname","created":"2026-11-18T08:05:22","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4587864426,"indicator":"motus.relayconsolidation.online","type":"hostname","created":"2026-11-18T08:05:22","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4587864427,"indicator":"motus.iconnectdataconsolidation.online","type":"hostname","created":"2026-11-18T08:05:22","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4587864433,"indicator":"56970620ba88b24aa993099cebbe7d5e118447b52450e886f9f896abc88ceab0","type":"FileHash-SHA256","created":"2026-11-18T08:05:22","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4589822943,"indicator":"discovery.foundation.forum","type":"hostname","created":"2026-11-18T08:05:22","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null}],"tags":["castlerat","broker impersonation","noderemote","webdav delivery","meshcentral","carrier verification","logistics targeting","fuel card theft","remote access trojan","netsupport manager","credential harvesting","nightshadec2","phishing portals"],"targeted_countries":["United States of America"],"malware_families":["NodeRemote","CastleRAT","NightshadeC2","MeshCentral","NetSupport Manager"],"attack_ids":["T1053.005","T1548.002","T1204.002","T1566.002","T1140","T1219","T1583.001","T1055","T1112","T1555.003","T1552.004","T1059.001","T1547.001","T1562.001","T1027","T1573","T1132","T1071.001","T1059.005","T1021.001","T1204.001"],"references":["https:\/\/any.run\/cybersecurity-blog\/us-logistics-cyber-threats-3-campaigns\/"],"industries":["Transportation"],"extract_source":[],"more_indicators":false},{"id":"6afd5d540e49984e613c22ce","name":"agent-framework Compromised: Credential Stealer Targets Azure and CI Pipelines","description":"On November 17, 2026, two malicious versions (1.26.1 and 1.26.2) of Microsoft's agent-framework Python package were published to PyPI for approximately 50 minutes before removal. The compromised packages deployed credential stealers through Python .pth files that executed automatically on interpreter startup. The malware targeted Azure and CI\/CD environments, extracting environment variables containing secrets, credential files from Azure CLI, Docker, Git, and package managers, plus Azure managed-identity and OIDC tokens. Version 1.26.2 enhanced capabilities to steal GitHub Actions OIDC tokens from workflows with federated credential access. Stolen data was exfiltrated via a hardcoded webhook.site URL. The root cause appears to be unauthorized direct upload to PyPI outside the normal release process, though this has not been confirmed.","author_name":"AlienVault","modified":"2026-11-18T09:32:26.925000","created":"2026-11-18T08:09:56.613000","revision":4,"tlp":"white","public":1,"adversary":"","indicators":[{"id":4589503135,"indicator":"d27fa34414e6201d5e03e559ef634f020057554d7b3f4898dd5d7cd3e989e110","type":"FileHash-SHA256","created":"2026-11-18T08:09:57","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4589503136,"indicator":"3d20a8bc91351a9a16b6db243b848ceca0206b7a8623b02d2af553a9c9f7e0a9","type":"FileHash-SHA256","created":"2026-11-18T08:09:57","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4589503137,"indicator":"https:\/\/webhook.site\/d381fd80-ec62-42ad-8f5c-d1b15103c9bb","type":"URL","created":"2026-11-18T09:32:18","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":""},{"id":4589503138,"indicator":"54d885b7d7161c9ed96489c66364c4bfbf635929166843bba10d97d46b5a2e1f","type":"FileHash-SHA256","created":"2026-11-18T08:09:57","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4589503139,"indicator":"325e7e9f0ec94e41ad1a1b7a3f18a6b8b5bffece2e2b97b8d3369eb967452f93","type":"FileHash-SHA256","created":"2026-11-18T08:09:57","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4589823126,"indicator":"0a013e4724c4437cf9b177def1d988113e167539","type":"FileHash-SHA1","created":"2026-11-18T08:09:57","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null}],"tags":["ci\/cd pipelines","azure credential theft","supply chain attack","github actions","pypi compromise","azure devops","oidc token theft","managed identity","python package"],"targeted_countries":[],"malware_families":[],"attack_ids":[],"references":["https:\/\/www.wiz.io\/blog\/malicious-version-of-microsofts-agent-framework-published-to-pypi"],"industries":[],"extract_source":[],"more_indicators":false},{"id":"6afd5d22755125a9b65a6dcb","name":"Active DGA Phishing and Polymorphic WebView Trojans Targeting Romanian Users - NACE Exchange \/ TroveX","description":"A sophisticated financial fraud campaign is actively targeting Romanian users through fake cryptocurrency exchange platforms branded as NACE Exchange and TroveX. The operation employs domain generation algorithms to rapidly rotate phishing domains that mimic legitimate crypto exchanges, harvesting credentials and personal data. Malicious Android APK files and iOS provisioning profiles are distributed as fake trading applications, functioning as WebView wrappers with embedded tracking infrastructure. These trojans request extensive permissions including GPS location tracking, clipboard access, contacts, and storage to exfiltrate sensitive data. The campaign has been documented across multiple European countries and utilizes personas like Professor Herbert Phillip. Infrastructure endpoints are frequently rotated to evade detection, making this a persistent transnational threat.","author_name":"AlienVault","modified":"2026-11-18T09:19:46.517000","created":"2026-11-18T08:09:06.686000","revision":2,"tlp":"white","public":1,"adversary":"","indicators":[{"id":4589823118,"indicator":"9005b2938f5b016a12a17a034be60474","type":"FileHash-MD5","created":"2026-11-18T08:09:07","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4589823119,"indicator":"d95ab974ef1d8b0eff8ec9b30198cffc","type":"FileHash-MD5","created":"2026-11-18T08:09:07","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4589823120,"indicator":"28fa03cc8baedb05548c105c1683daa2a34ca5a0","type":"FileHash-SHA1","created":"2026-11-18T08:09:07","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4589823121,"indicator":"58c13de7cdd919d4bb414a282213b9284c023849","type":"FileHash-SHA1","created":"2026-11-18T08:09:07","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4589823122,"indicator":"047d20f53c60708d3dd638c973b6d7d97b8d3f38426466c64a409ee4af949ab7","type":"FileHash-SHA256","created":"2026-11-18T08:09:07","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4589823123,"indicator":"3637e3b4402c935185c62258fa8e3718184470f92467d3cc9fc119fec2752606","type":"FileHash-SHA256","created":"2026-11-18T08:09:07","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4589823124,"indicator":"52a1c0733e4e4306a8f708a95a40c14e6f6c099e4590fbf5c9ad240b206e1439","type":"FileHash-SHA256","created":"2026-11-18T08:09:07","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null}],"tags":["dga phishing","android malware","trovex","webview trojan","nace exchange","android.riskware.spyagent.rb","cryptocurrency fraud","ios malware","romanian targeting"],"targeted_countries":["Romania"],"malware_families":["Android.Riskware.SpyAgent.RB"],"attack_ids":["T1583","T1204.002","T1566.002","T1106","T1608.001","T1583.001","T1036","T1204","T1566"],"references":["https:\/\/community.bitdefender.com\/en\/discussion\/107250\/active-threat-intelligence-report-dga-phishing-polymorphic-webview-trojans-targeting-romanian-users-nace-exchange-trovex"],"industries":["Finance"],"extract_source":[],"more_indicators":false},{"id":"6afd5a8a1dc37870181386de","name":"Hackers Exploit Critical ScreenConnect Flaw to Silently Run Malware on MSP Technicians' Computers","description":"Attackers are exploiting CVE-2026-84869, a critical vulnerability in ScreenConnect with a CVSS score of 9.9, to execute malicious files on managed service provider technician workstations without user confirmation. The flaw allows malicious guests to send files during remote support sessions and trigger execution with elevated privileges. In a documented November 12 incident, attackers installed a rogue remote access client in approximately nine seconds. Researchers identified over 688,000 delivery attempts across 42 MSP servers between October and November, originating from 29 IP addresses. The attack chain involves batch scripts, PowerShell commands, and installation of disguised ScreenConnect clients connecting to attacker-controlled infrastructure. Affected organizations must update technician clients to version 26.6.5 or later and investigate suspicious file transfers and executions.","author_name":"AlienVault","modified":"2026-11-18T07:59:38.975000","created":"2026-11-18T07:58:02.864000","revision":2,"tlp":"white","public":1,"adversary":"","indicators":[{"id":2129894116,"indicator":"194.15.36.33","type":"IPv4","created":"2026-11-18T07:58:03","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":"2026-12-18T07:00:00","is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4065021202,"indicator":"38.18.228.173","type":"IPv4","created":"2026-11-18T07:58:03","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":"2026-12-18T07:00:00","is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4402075842,"indicator":"172.81.61.149","type":"IPv4","created":"2026-11-18T07:58:03","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":"2026-12-18T07:00:00","is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4476408427,"indicator":"38.18.228.165","type":"IPv4","created":"2026-11-18T07:58:03","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":"2026-12-18T07:00:00","is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4494872864,"indicator":"CVE-2026-84869","type":"CVE","created":"2026-11-18T07:58:03","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4573772233,"indicator":"masterdarky.com","type":"domain","created":"2026-11-18T07:58:03","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4587314805,"indicator":"f8871b1561d5c77c297378a7f49c84de52a01ff297395544f0e95d13ef972841","type":"FileHash-SHA256","created":"2026-11-18T07:58:03","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_act